THIRD PARTY NOTICES
===================

This file lists third-party components distributed with Mirador binaries or
sources, as required by the design document (sections 21-22) and the project
standards (docs/project/project-standards.md, section 9).

1. GoogleTest (https://github.com/google/googletest)

   Included as the pinned submodule third_party/googletest (v1.18.0,
   commit 063de7e9578f82b369302001269680b4b1553359). Used exclusively by the
   test suite; it is never linked into mirador-core or shipped artifacts.
   License: BSD-3-Clause. Copyright 2008, Google Inc.
   Full text: third_party/googletest/LICENSE
   Audit record: docs/supply-chain/googletest.md

As of 2026-09-13 this is the only third-party component in the repository; the
Mirador core itself depends only on the C++20 standard library.

2. OpenCV (https://opencv.org) - integrator-provided, not distributed

   Used exclusively by the optional adapter adapters/opencv (M1-09) behind the
   CMake option MIRADOR_BUILD_ADAPTERS_OPENCV (default OFF). OpenCV is never
   vendored into this repository and never distributed with Mirador sources or
   binaries: integrators provide their own OpenCV build through
   find_package(OpenCV) and take on the license obligations of the OpenCV they
   link. License: Apache License 2.0 (OpenCV 4.x). Versions tested by the
   Mirador project: 4.6.0 (Ubuntu 24.04 apt package). Only opencv_core is
   required; only the cv::Mat data/step/type surface is consumed.

Optional modules may introduce pinned dependencies (for example ELSED). Each
such dependency, its pinned version, license and source must be recorded here
and in docs/supply-chain/ before it is distributed; license review must
complete before ELSED or similar algorithm sources are vendored.

Model runtimes (ncnn, ONNX Runtime, MNN, TensorRT, ...) and model weights are
never distributed with the core library. Backend examples for specific
runtimes live in separate repositories or in integrations/ that the default
build must not fetch. See docs/design/mirador-development-design.md for the
full boundary description.

3. ncnn (https://github.com/Tencent/ncnn) - opt-in integrations, never
   distributed with the core

   Used exclusively by the reference capability backends under integrations/
   (M5-02, DEC-015) behind the CMake option MIRADOR_BUILD_INTEGRATIONS
   (default OFF). ncnn is never vendored into this repository: the default
   build does not fetch, compile or link it, and the Mirador core release
   never carries it. When the option is ON, the pinned release
   20260526 (commit e54f7b1f88434e1d844ea0551b880a1cfb079ce1) is fetched from
   the upstream repository at configure time into the build tree. Anyone who
   compiles and distributes the integrations backends distributes ncnn and
   takes on its obligations: License: BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2017
   Tencent. Full text: upstream LICENSE file of the pinned commit. Audit
   record: docs/supply-chain/ncnn.md.
